        "date": "2026-01-30T20:25:14Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(data): add Semihosting non-ISA specification\n\nAdd the RISC-V Semihosting specification as a non-ISA specification\nfollowing the non_isa_schema.json format.\n\nSemihosting allows applications running in debug/simulation environments\nto access host system resources (console, file system, time, etc.) through\na special instruction sequence:\n- slli x0, x0, 0x1f  (Entry NOP)\n- ebreak             (Break to debugger)\n- srai x0, x0, 7     (Exit NOP)\n\nThis is the first standard non-ISA specification in spec/std/non_isa/.\n\nThe specification includes:\n- Description of the semihosting concept and design rationale\n- Breakpoint instruction sequence requirements (normative)\n- Parameter passing convention via a0/a1 registers (normative)\n- Overview of available semihosting services\n- References to official specification and ARM semihosting spec\n\nCloses #1393",
